<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">West Francia</h1><p class="st-meta">843 CE – 987 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Western third of the Carolingian realm, created at Verdun in 843, out of which the Kingdom of France grew.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After civil war among the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843 gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> the lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>. His realm took in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/neustria">Neustria</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marca-hispanica">Spanish March</a>, though <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Brittany</a> remained largely independent.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Royal power weakened under the pressure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raids and of great regional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> who turned their offices into hereditary principalities. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> ordered fortified bridges in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-pitres">Edict of Pîtres</a> in 864. Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-of-france">Odo of Paris</a> defended the city against the Vikings in 885 to 886 and was elected king, beginning a rivalry between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a> and his Robertian family.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 911 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a> the land that became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Duchy of Normandy</a>. Kings alternated between the two families until the last Carolingian, Louis V, died in 987, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/west-francia.jpg" alt="West Francia" width="320" height="243"><figcaption>Image: Blank map of Europe.svg: maix¿? derivative work: Alphathon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Francia_843.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>843 CE – 987 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles the Bald, Odo, Charles the Simple</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Francia Occidentalis, Kingdom of the West Franks</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=915&amp;focus=west-francia" aria-label="West Francia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where West Francia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5139 672M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5035 888M5054 728L5139 672M5054 728L5144 875M5054 728L4930 753M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5025 711M5054 728L5118 774M5054 728L5035 888M5054 728L5035 888M5054 728L5073 659M5054 728L5075 699"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5054 728h0M5035 888h0M5139 672h0M5144 875h0M4930 753h0M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5025 711h0M5118 774h0M5035 888h0M5035 888h0M5073 659h0M5075 699h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=915&amp;focus=west-francia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
